engine: also build the gl4es renderer for the web

The fork's Emscripten configure enables only the webgl2 target (gl2_shim).
gl4es is in the tree, knows about Emscripten in its own sources and
CMake, and is the more mature GL-to-GLES translator. Build it beside the
shim so the two can be measured against each other; the page picks with
-ref. An experiment; if it does not compile, that is the result.

--- a/wscript
+++ b/wscript
@@ -264,6 +264,7 @@
 	elif conf.options.EMSCRIPTEN:
 		conf.options.GL               = False
 		conf.options.WEBGL2           = True
+		conf.options.GL4ES            = True
 
 	if conf.options.DLL_LOADER or conf.env.DEST_OS == 'win32' or conf.env.DEST_OS == 'android':
 		conf.options.SUPPORT_BSP2_FORMAT = False
